WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.980
Koikimo

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:08.280
Hey, Rio.

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:11.240
Is Ryo-san on a business trip or something?

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.450
Huh? No.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:16.190
I see. Then is he feeling okay?

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.340
I think so. What's wrong?

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.450
It's not a big deal.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.780
It's just that he hasn't called 
me since our flower viewing.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.210
I was just wondering if he's okay.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:30.140
Wait, hold up. My brother was 
still calling you every day?

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.220
I'm not sure if I should 
be scared or impressed...

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.220
He really kept that up for six months...

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:36.700
Now that you mention it... 
I guess it has been six months.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.600
Before, any time he couldn't call, 
he'd always let me know in advance,

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.200
so I was a little worried.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.210
Then why don't you try calling him?

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:48.040
What?

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.070
You're worried, aren't you? Call him.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.400
Uh... Hmm...

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.360
<b>Chemistry Lab</b>

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:55.360
But, I mean...

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.870
Maybe Ryo-san has a good 
reason he can't call.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:03.370
And you'll need to call him to find that out.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.110
Uh...

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:06.670
Listen...

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.120
You like my brother, don't you?

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:15.010
I've been trying to be nice about this,

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:19.100
but if you're going to be half-assed 
about it, I feel bad for my brother.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:22.820
You need to make up your mind already.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:29.980
Episode 12

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:29.980
"You're Creepy"

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:31.480
Wait.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:33.480
It's April, isn't it?

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.430
Ichika?

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.110
Yeah, it is.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:41.640
Oh, dear. Dad's birthday 
is right around the corner.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.200
Oh, you're right! I still need to buy him a gift!

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.750
Yeah, I totally forgot...

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:49.580
How old is Dad going to be?

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.710
Forty... something?

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:57.930
Hey, how many years apart are you two again?

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:58.680
Huh?

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.780
Let's see...

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:04.890
Your father's five years older.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:07.520
Five years...

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:13.600
Once you become an adult, though, 
five years is really nothing.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.690
Yeah, at your age.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.360
At my age...

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.030
Five years is pretty big.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.370
Well, for you right now, yes.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:27.300
But you'll be an adult before you know it.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.250
Nothing special. No big deal.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.550
It's not?

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:33.770
Nope!

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.820
What? You want to be an adult already?

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:41.080
Maybe that's it.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.270
I wonder if he'll wait for 
me until I'm an adult.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.110
What are you talking about?

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:49.710
Ow.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.730
You need to put in some effort 
so he'll wait for you.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:57.230
He's a great guy, so he may just disappear 
if you don't put in any effort.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:02.730
Uh, Mom... Do you know what 
I'm actually talking about?

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:03.530
Really?

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:06.500
I was going to overlook that part, 
but you're really asking?

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:10.520
Moms are scary.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:18.260
< Frequently used contacts

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:18.260
Ryo-san

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:18.260
Rio

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:18.260
tsuki

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:18.260
Ruri

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:18.260
Mom

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.630
<i>I couldn't tell him how I really 
felt at the flower viewing.</i>

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.510
<   Frequently used contacts

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.510
Ryo-san

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.510
Rio

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:26.230
I need to make up my mind... put in effort...

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.240
Ichika-san

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.450
<i>Hello?</i>

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.000
Oh, hello?

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.680
It's been a while.

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:54.460
<i>It has.</i>

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.710
May I asked why you called?

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.590
Oh, right.

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:05.550
Someone gave me two 
tickets to the art museum.

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:07.850
So, um...

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:12.180
<i>Will you go with me n-next Saturday?</i>

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:16.720
<i>Um...</i>

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.320
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.490
<i>I have to work that day.</i>

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.730
Oh, I see.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.250
Then how about Sunday?

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:30.840
I have plans on Sunday, too. I'm sorry.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.210
<i>Oh, it's fine. Don't worry about it.</i>

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:36.130
You haven't been contacting me much lately.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.460
Did something happen?

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.010
I've been really swamped with work. I'm sorry.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.930
<i>Oh, it's okay. You have no control over that.</i>

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:47.320
Also...

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.140
I won't be able to call you for a while.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:53.060
Even if you call me, I don't 
think I'll be able to answer.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.900
Oh... really?

00:04:58.450 --> 00:04:59.900
I'm sorry.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:02.860
<i>I'm still at work, so... I'm going to hang up.</i>

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:06.280
Oh, I'm sorry! Good luck at work!

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.310
<i>G-Goodbye.</i>

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:21.030
And if you start with C...

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.180
< Frequently used contacts

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.180
Ryo-san

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.180
Rio

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.180
Satsuki

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.180
Ruri

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.180
Mom

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.660
<i>It really has been a while</i>

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:41.610
<i>since I last talked to Ryo-san.</i>

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:54.610
<i>I forgot to buy a notebook.</i>

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:56.890
<i>Oh, well. I'll buy one later.</i>

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:01.720
<i>Ryo-san!</i>

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.860
I think that'll be perfectly fine.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:09.180
We can cover the rest at next week's meeting.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.320
Right. Thank you very much.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:13.720
<i>Sounds like he's doing work stuff.</i>

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.740
<i>I shouldn't interrupt.</i>

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:31.300
I'll send you the documents via email.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.980
Thank you. I'll take a look later.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:38.020
I'll be showing the email to the 
rest of my department, as well.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.080
Sorry I took so long.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.480
Took you long enough!

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:38.830
Sorry, my bad.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.060
Is that all right, Amakusa-san?

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:42.970
Amakusa-san?

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:44.840
Oh, yes.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:47.040
Thank you very much.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.540
Likewise.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.020
Ichika. Ichika.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.180
Ichika!

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:02.020
Huh?

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.340
What?

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:04.390
Order.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:06.520
Let's see...

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:11.160
Did you try calling my brother?

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:14.750
Um... Yeah, I did.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.170
And?

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:18.080
And... nothing, really.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.040
What's that supposed to mean?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.090
Nothing.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.460
He seemed really busy.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:28.870
Busy?

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:32.010
Yeah. He said he wouldn't 
be able to call for a while.

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:35.510
I'll ask him what's going on.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:36.720
Huh? No, that's okay.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:38.480
But this hasn't happened before.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:41.120
He never used work as an 
excuse to distance himself.

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:45.330
Yeah, but... If he's really 
busy, what can we do?

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:46.090
But—

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:47.330
Just don't!

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:50.490
Rio, you're meddling too much!

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:53.950
What's that supposed to mean?

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.260
It's because you two weren't 
making any progress.

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:58.620
B-But that's my choice!

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.090
That doesn't concern you!

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:05.370
Sorry I'm so annoying.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.090
That's not—

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:18.850
I do like Ryo-san.

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:24.700
But I'm not a good match for him.

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:26.520
We're far apart in age, too.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:30.660
I'm sure there's someone more suited for him.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:33.530
A good match for him? Like who?

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:39.540
Um... Someone who's mature, 
pretty, fashionable, and smart...

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.810
This new lipstick I bought is great!

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.540
Really? Maybe I'll buy it, too.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.500
Huh... So that's how you feel.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:45.460
Then maybe there is someone.

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:49.900
I don't see any need to think that way, though.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.920
Those are just some rando's standards.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:58.710
My brother likes you, and you like him back.

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:00.100
Isn't that enough?

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:05.410
Besides, you can be more mature, 
and you can be fashionable if you want.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:08.560
Did my brother ever say he 
liked someone like that?

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.650
No, but...

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:14.040
You're probably only thinking this 
because you lack confidence.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:15.850
Well...

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:22.490
At first, I just thought it'd be 
sorta fun if you two went out.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:27.870
But then some things changed for the 
better after he started liking you.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:32.170
Now I can tell that you two 
actually like each other,

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.100
and that's why I want to support you two.

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:39.530
Having my precious older brother go 
out with my precious best friend...

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:42.540
would be the best.

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:47.830
Rio...

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.360
I was trying to hold back 
a little more, but...

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:54.530
I said too much. I'm sorry.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:57.970
No, it's okay! I'm sorry for 
saying this didn't concern you!

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:01.040
Don't apologize. You should thank me instead.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:04.350
It's all thanks to me that 
you two met each other.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.660
Just kidding.

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:08.470
Thank you.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:14.000
I'll meet Ryo-san in person 
and tell him how I feel.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:17.460
I'll try to get him to see me somehow.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.340
Good.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:27.980
<b>Adabi</b>

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:30.580
Good evening.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:37.490
You seem down in the dumps for once.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.010
What's up? Did something happen?

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:02.990
Ichika-san asked me out 
on a date the other day.

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:05.110
Oh, my goodness! Well, congratulations!

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:06.150
But I turned her down.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.020
What? Why?

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.630
I lied to her and said 
that I was busy with work.

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:12.590
No, really. Why, though?

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:16.340
I thought I'd back off...

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:19.150
Huh?!

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:24.260
Lately, it feels like Ichika-san might 
actually have some feelings for me.

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:25.910
Okay, and?

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:30.690
And when I realized that... I sorta 
got scared, for several reasons.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.490
I remembered how I used to be and got scared.

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:40.760
Am I someone who can actually 
take care of Ichika-san?

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:43.880
Am I a decent adult who 
can take responsibility?

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:48.970
Most importantly, I don't 
want Ichika-san to suffer.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:53.650
So I thought that maybe I should 
just back off... for good.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:04.290
Masuda, are you even listening?

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:07.340
Ryo, are you being serious right now?

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:08.540
Of course I am.

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:11.870
I see.

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:16.330
Mind if I slug you, then?

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:17.670
Wha?

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.340
God, you're lame!

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:21.380
You're being so lame right now!

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:26.140
It's not fair for you to run away now, after 
everything you put Ichika-chan through!

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:30.620
Were you lying about being 
prepared to be hurt?

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:34.140
If you keep running like this, 
Ichika-chan really is going to disappear!

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:36.270
Are you really okay with that?

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:40.810
Absolutely not.

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:42.530
Right?

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:47.740
Besides, if you don't want to hurt 
someone who's important to you,

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.900
then you just need to work harder.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.930
The more I feel that Ichika-san is dear to me,

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:56.330
the more I don't know what I should do.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:01.830
You're actually able to reflect on yourself,

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:04.010
meaning you'd be able to put 
in the necessary effort.

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:07.420
You need to face Ichika-chan head-on.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:16.200
And that was my dose of tough 
love! Well? Did it hurt?

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:18.060
Yeah, actually.

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:22.030
But I've been avoiding 
Ichika-san this whole time...

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:25.800
Wouldn't I be an ass if I reached 
out to her first, at this point?

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:30.910
<b>Gloom...</b>

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:30.600
People would never guess that you're 
actually pretty earnest and awkward.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:33.920
You're really being a bully today.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:37.250
That's so rude. I'm just 
giving you the push you need.

00:13:38.990 --> 00:13:40.250
Well, thanks.

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:46.560
Er, I have no idea how to respond 
when you thank me like that.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:48.220
That's exactly why I did it.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:49.260
You suck.

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:50.690
Here you go.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:53.560
Huh? But we didn't order this.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:54.600
It's on the house.

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:08.660
Yeah, I found the black binder.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.690
It was in one of your desk drawers.

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:13.160
<i>Oh, so that's where it was.</i>

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:16.380
<i>Just leave it on my desk.
I'll come get it tomorrow.</i>

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:17.620
Okay.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.260
Onii-chan.

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:23.320
<i>Hmm? What is it?</i>

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:28.470
I'll meet Ryo-san and person 
and tell him how I feel.

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:32.220
Nah, never mind.

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:34.310
Rio.

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:36.910
<i>Thanks.</i>

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:40.350
You're always there to give me the push I need.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:42.530
<i>I'll talk to you later.</i>

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:01.090
Dad.

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:02.790
Yes?

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.900
I want you to be there for Onii-chan.

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:09.120
Please.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:22.730
< Ichika

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:22.730
Ichika

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:22.730
I'm going to try to call 
Ryo-san after school today.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:22.730
I'll do my best to try to make plans to meet with him.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:22.730
<b>I'll do my best!</b>

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:27.370
You've got this.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:31.990
<b>Touch Firmly</b>

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.110
<b>Tap</b>

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:33.240
<b>Touch Firmly</b>

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:33.240
<b>Tap</b>

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:43.070
Ryo-san.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.520
<i>No... I...</i>

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:05.770
<i>I can't run away from my feelings</i>

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:07.610
<i>anymore!</i>

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.700
Pardon me. Please let me through!

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:20.470
I'm so sorry!

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:24.830
Ryo-san!

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:29.170
Wait!

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:34.650
Ryo-san...

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:54.060
Ryo-san!

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:00.010
Ichika-san...

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:05.960
I finally found you...

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:18.580
Are you all right?

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:23.100
Why were you avoiding me?!

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:24.210
Huh?

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:26.190
You haven't contacted at me at all lately,

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:29.020
and then you indirectly told me 
not to contact you, either!

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:31.980
I was worried that you might be sick!

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:35.830
I'm sorry.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:37.700
As you can see, I'm fine.

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.800
Answer my question!

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:47.920
I wasn't sure if I should 
stay by your side anymore.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:51.170
Staying by your side forever...

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:53.220
I have the resolve to do that.

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:57.340
But all this time, I've just been 
forcing my feelings onto you,

00:17:57.740 --> 00:18:00.470
and I've made things difficult for you.

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:04.630
I'm probably going to keep 
causing you even more trouble.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:09.150
So maybe I shouldn't be by your side.

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:12.390
These thoughts just kept running 
through my mind over and over...

00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:15.280
And here I am.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:25.930
What's that supposed to mean?

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:30.540
You're basically completely 
ignoring my feelings.

00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:34.100
You don't get to decide how I feel!

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:37.740
I can't even argue with that.

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:39.250
And...

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:43.330
It's even harder for me 
not having you around.

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:44.750
I see.

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:45.460
Huh?

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:48.660
I finally figured it out.

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:52.950
Do you remember the first time we met?

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:54.230
Of course.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:56.290
I saved you here,

00:18:56.290 --> 00:19:00.820
then was reunited with you and found 
out that you were Rio's older brother.

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:03.000
Then you said the worst thing ever to me.

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:05.200
I did.

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:09.160
Without thinking, I called you creepy.

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:12.610
Then you suddenly asked 
me out in such a bold way.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:17.410
You really were nothing but 
trouble in the beginning.

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:21.200
But your feelings were so straightforward...

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:25.050
And I started to understand that you 
were actually earnest and a bit awkward.

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:28.950
Any time I asked Rio for advice, 
it ended up being about you.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:33.360
And then I suddenly realized 
that I was thinking about you.

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:38.060
You did nothing but cause me trouble...

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:41.770
You're annoying, gaudy, and on the 
verge of committing a crime...

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:44.240
You rub it in my face that 
you're handsome and smart...

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:47.660
You're self-centered... 
You're basically filled with flaws!

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:48.720
But...

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.090
I love you.

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:55.690
I love you, Ryo-san.

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:14.590
Yes. I love you, too, Ichika-san.

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:17.150
Wh-Wha...

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:19.130
What do you think you're doing?!

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:22.180
I'm sorry. I was just so happy 
that I couldn't hold back.

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:23.150
What?!

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:26.330
I had no idea that you loved 
me so much, Ichika-san.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:29.110
I really hate that you're 
saying it like that.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:30.850
And yet you love me anyway.

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:33.290
God, I hate to admit it, but I guess so.

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:40.300
I'm sorry I was avoiding you.

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:44.570
And thank you for chasing after me.

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:47.840
Ryo-san...

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:48.620
Yes?

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:53.300
Will you wait for me until I'm an adult?

00:20:57.820 --> 00:20:58.820
Yes.

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:01.770
We can take all the time you need together.

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:11.410
And if I do anything wrong, 
I want you to yell at me.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:14.730
I love it when you yell at me.

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:16.400
What's that supposed to mean?

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:20.780
You're so creepy.

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:28.720
Ichika

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:31.500
Hello?

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.490
Are you going back to your place?

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:43.290
I just came by to get something I forgot.

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:48.400
About what we discussed the other day...

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:52.870
I plan to wait for Ichika-san 
until she's an adult.

00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:57.620
I know that I've done plenty of things 
to make you doubt my intentions,

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:00.810
so I understand why you'd 
be against this. I get it.

00:22:01.850 --> 00:22:05.130
But I changed when I met Ichika-san.

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:08.550
I plan to stay by her side 
once she becomes an adult,

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:12.210
and I'm going to protect her 
because she's precious to me.

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:15.020
I hope you can understand that.

00:22:16.810 --> 00:22:19.500
Anyway, I'm going back to my place.

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:26.920
He's so stubborn.

00:22:27.370 --> 00:22:28.610
Yes.

00:22:29.150 --> 00:22:30.740
He's just like you.

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:34.710
<i>I don't regret</i>

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:39.120
<i>what I did for him that day.</i>

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:52.780
<i>As for what I said to him that day...</i>

00:22:52.780 --> 00:22:54.200
<i>I have nothing but regrets.</i>

00:23:30.170 --> 00:23:34.130
<i>Because "creepy" somehow turned into "love."</i>
